OmniGibson 3.9.0 (StanfordVL/BEHAVIOR-1K v3.9.0, 6559858) on Isaac Sim 6.1 / Kit 110 (Python 3.12,
torch 2.11 cu128, warp 1.16). Applied by install_isaac61.sh at the BEHAVIOR-1K root; run on the box's
RTX 5090 with driver 595.71.05, where OmniGibson's own Isaac Sim 5.1 segfaults at RTX startup
(isaac-sim/IsaacSim#677).

- simulator.py: an omnigibson_6_1_0.kit for Isaac Sim 6.1.0 (OmniGibson picks its kit file by the
  exact Isaac Sim version); the PhysX interface and PhysX simulation interface come from omni.physx
  (Isaac Sim 6.1's PhysicsContext no longer keeps _physx_interface / _physx_sim_interface).
- omnigibson_6_1_0.kit: omnigibson_5_1_0.kit with Kit 110's extension registry. The deprecated
  isaacsim.core.* extensions OmniGibson uses still ship (extsDeprecated) and load through
  isaacsim.exp.base.
- prims/material_prim.py: OpenUSD without Ndr renamed SdrShaderNode.GetInput / GetInputNames to
  GetShaderInput / GetShaderInputNames (old names kept as the fallback).
- utils/deprecated_utils.py: Isaac Sim 6.1 invalidates an articulation's physics view through
  carb.eventdispatcher (GLOBAL_EVENT_STOP only, events without .type).
- action_primitives/curobo.py: an OmniGibson 3.9.0 bug on compute capability 12.0 (RTX 50-series),
  not an Isaac Sim 6.1 one: CuRoboMotionGenerator drops the R1Pro's DEFAULT embodiment there (its
  warmup hits a CUDA illegal memory access in cuRobo's optimizer; reproduced with cuRobo built for
  sm_120), then update_obstacles indexed the missing DEFAULT MotionGen, so every plan raised
  KeyError. It now updates the shared world collision checker through the MotionGen that exists.

Not changed, measured: Kit renders on the one GPU CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES leaves visible when
OMNIGIBSON_GPU_ID is unset (the env server's sim.set_render_gpu); an explicit active_gpu 0 makes
RTX create no device on Isaac Sim 6.1.

